          "lineage": "Araeonema",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Additional material. 73 specimens from ' Marohn' (Locality 28), 2 from Glenbawn (Locality 29) and 1 from ' Lorrina' (Locality 23). Geographic distribution. ' Lorrina' to Glenbawn. Geological age. Late Tournaisian. Remarks. This species has a very thin shell, yet is extremely well preserved. It is one of the most abundant species at the type locality. A single worn specimen recovered from the upper part of the Namoi Formation at ' Lorrina' is tentatively referred to this species.",
